# What must NOT be sent to the Docker daemon.
#
# This file is a security control as much as a speed one. Everything listed
# here would otherwise be copied into the build context by `COPY . .` — and
# a file that reaches the builder can end up in an image layer, where it
# stays readable forever even if a later layer deletes it.
#
# The two that matter most are `.env` and `keys/`. A private signing key
# baked into an image is a key you have published to everyone who can pull
# it.

# Secrets — never, under any circumstances.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
keys/
*.pem

# Reinstalled inside the image, for the right platform. Copying the host's
# node_modules would also copy native modules compiled for Windows.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — rebuilt in the builder stage. Copying it risks shipping a
# stale bundle that nothing in the image explains.
dist
tmp
out-tsc

# Caches, none of which mean anything inside a container.
.nx
.angular
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local tooling and history.
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.claude
*.log

# Documentation and test assets. They change constantly, and every change
# would otherwise invalidate the Docker layer cache for no reason.
docs
postman
README.md
*.md
